{"title":"Career: Agricultural Officer","role":"Agricultural Officer","summary":"Role: An Agricultural Officer works at the intersection of agriculture, engineering, farm technology, rural development, and agricultural administration. The role may involve supporting farmers, implementing government agricultural schemes, promoting modern farming practices, assessing crop and farm conditions, coordinating agricultural programmes, and advising on irrigation, mechanisation, soil and water management.","facts":{},"about":[{"label":"Direct alignment","text":"Very High. Agricultural Engineering provides strong technical knowledge in farm machinery, irrigation, soil and water engineering, agricultural processing, renewable energy, and farm management. For an Agricultural Officer role, this should be supplemented with agricultural economics, extension services, government schemes, rural development, crop science, and public administration."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Agricultural engineering + crop/agriculture fundamentals + government exam preparation"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Agricultural Officer / field officer / agricultural development roles"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Senior officer, programme implementation, agricultural technology management"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"District/state-level administration, agricultural policy, agri-tech leadership or specialist roles"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Agriculture & Engineering Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Core subjects"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Engineering Mathematics"},{"text":"Engineering Physics"},{"text":"Engineering Chemistry"},{"text":"Fundamentals of Agriculture"},{"text":"Botany / Crop Science"},{"text":"Soil Science"},{"text":"Engineering Drawing"},{"text":"Basic Computing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Build knowledge of"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Major Indian crops"},{"text":"Cropping seasons"},{"text":"Kharif/Rabi/Zaid"},{"text":"Basic soil types"},{"text":"Agricultural regions"},{"text":"Farm operations"},{"text":"Rural economy"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"Data collection"},{"text":"Technical report writing"},{"text":"Basic statistics"},{"text":"Field observation"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Outcome","text":"Understand both the engineering and agricultural sides of farming."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Farm Engineering & Resource Management"},{"type":"h","text":"Core areas"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Soil and Water Engineering"},{"text":"Farm Machinery"},{"text":"Agricultural Power"},{"text":"Irrigation Engineering"},{"text":"Surveying"},{"text":"Crop Production"},{"text":"Agricultural Meteorology"},{"text":"Agricultural Economics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical skills"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Irrigation-system design"},{"text":"Soil-water analysis"},{"text":"Farm machinery operation"},{"text":"Basic CAD"},{"text":"Land surveying"},{"text":"Agricultural data collection"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"GIS fundamentals"},{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"GPS/GNSS basics"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Outcome","text":"Become capable of analysing agricultural land, water, machinery and farm-resource requirements."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Agricultural Systems & Field Administration"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Farm Management"},{"text":"Agricultural Extension"},{"text":"Agricultural Economics"},{"text":"Watershed Management"},{"text":"Post-harvest Technology"},{"text":"Agricultural Processing"},{"text":"Renewable Energy in Agriculture"},{"text":"Precision Agriculture"},{"text":"Remote Sensing"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Rural Development"}]},{"type":"h","tex